# Strategy v2.0 Specification: DRAFT (freezes on Week 7 Day 2)

## Universe
- Current S&P 500 constituents (survivorship bias acknowledged in DATA_NOTES.md)
- A stock is eligible on a date only if all three signals are valid

## Signals (computed at month-end close, using data up to and including that day)
1. Momentum: close[t-21] / close[t-252] - 1
2. Low volatility: -(std of daily returns over the trailing 252 days)
3. Short-term reversal: -(close[t] / close[t-21] - 1)

## Standardisation
- Winsorise each signal at the 5th and 95th percentile across stocks, per date
- Cross-sectional z-score per date
- Combined score = equal-weighted average of the three z-scores

## Parameters
- 252, 21, 252, 5%/95%
- sensitivity to be tested later

## Checks done
- Look-ahead test passed on [N] random development-period dates


## Portfolio construction and execution
- Hold the top 15 names by combined score; equal dollar weight at each rebalance
- Rebalance monthly; signal at month-end close, executed at the NEXT trading day's close
- Backtest uses fractional shares (cash drag in whole-share mode: [your number])
- Between rebalances, positions drift; no intra-month trading
- Cash earns no interest (simplification). 
- n_holdings = 15 carried over from v1.0 as a convention, not tuned; sensitivity tested in Week 8



## Validation criteria (15/11/26 - before the validation run)

Window: 2022-01-01 to 2024-12-31. Weights: [W_FINAL]. Cost: 10 bps. Fresh start from cash.

Development sub-period reference ranges: Sharpe [min]-[max]; max drawdown worst [x]%;
beta [min]-[max].

- C1: validation net Sharpe >= [min dev sub-period Sharpe]
- C2: validation net CAGR minus equal-weight-universe net CAGR > 0
- C3: max drawdown not worse than [worst dev drawdown] + 5 percentage points
- C4: beta vs SPY within [min dev beta - 0.15, max dev beta + 0.15]
- C5: mean monthly rank IC of the combined score > 0 over the window

Verdict: HELD UP if C1, C2 and C5 all pass. DID NOT HOLD UP if net Sharpe <= 0, or if C2 and C5
both fail. Otherwise MIXED (report which criteria failed).


Known contamination: I saw v1.0's result on this window before designing v2.0.



## Transaction cost assumption (decided before any results)
- Base case: [10] bps per side, charged on traded notional (buys and sells)


## Week 8 Day 4: significance tests (before running)

Windows: development (2012-2021) and validation (2022-2024), reported separately. Holdout untouched.
Tests: (1) t-test of mean daily excess return vs 0; (2) analytic and block-bootstrap 95% CI for the
net Sharpe; (3) strategy vs equal-weight universe: paired block bootstrap of the Sharpe difference
and of annualised active return; (4) null-best-Sharpe comparison across a bracket of trial counts.
Conventions: 95% intervals, block length 21 days (sensitivity: 5 and 63), 3,000 resamples.

